--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@ original. Anything that cannot be derived from the b1.7.3 sources is marked
 | Voxel LoD (Voxy style) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (10 tests in `world::lod`, rewritten 2026-10-17) | `world/lod.rs`: far terrain out to 768 blocks as real 3D block columns (runs of equal blocks) of 64 x 64 tiles, meshed as voxels at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 / 16 blocks after a Voxy-style 2x2x2 mip (`Mipper`), faces only where a solid voxel meets a see-through one; same atlas, tints, face shades and fog as the chunks. **Real chunks first** (Voxy's ingest): `lod::columns`, `ChunkManager::take_ingest`, `Lod::ingest`. The cut under the ring only happens where a real chunk mesh exists (`ChunkManager::drawn`), so no hole to the sky. Trees are real trunk + crown voxels up to 420 blocks and a leaf carpet over dense forest beyond (2026-10-18), the terrain fog starts at 88% of the view, pre-generation runs from the start; terrain rounds to the step instead of bloating. See ROADMAP changelog. |
 | River merge + length (2026-10-24) | written without a full toolchain: the 16 `hydro::tests` (2 new) pass in a Linux scratch crate; the rest not compiled, not run | `world/gen/hydro.rs`: a stream joining a bigger river runs level with it (flat over the channel overlap, then rises to its own surface), and a source shorter than `MIN_LEN` 160 blocks before a confluence where it is not the biggest branch (or the sea) is dropped. See the world changelog. |
 | River steps (organic slope) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+3 tests: `hydro::tests::a_lower_river_does_not_overwrite_a_higher_one`, `ticks::tests::woken_edge_water_spreads_into_levels`, `chunks::tests::edge_water_is_a_surface_source_with_air_beside_it`) | A river from a neighbouring plate is no longer cut by a lower river's bank (`Region::plan_at`), and the still water at a step or a cut bank is woken like the mod's `scheduleTick` (`ChunkManager::edge_water`, `Ticks::wake_water`) so the fluid sim writes the slope as real levels. See ROADMAP changelog. |
-| M14 player model     | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+3 tests in `player.rs`, +1 in `touch_ui.rs`) | `render/player.rs`: b1.7.3 `ModelBiped` + `mob/char.png` with walk / sneak / riding / arm-swing animation, in the third-person view (new view button) and as the inventory preview. No armor, ears, cloak or hurt flash. See ROADMAP changelog. |
+| M14 player model     | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+3 tests in `player.rs`, +1 in `touch_ui.rs`) | `render/player.rs`: b1.7.3 `ModelBiped` + `mob/char.png` with walk / sneak / riding / arm-swing animation, in the third-person view (new view button) and as the inventory preview. No armor, ears, cloak or hurt flash. See ROADMAP changelog. Armor on the model (`armor_quads`: `RenderPlayer.setArmorModel`, the worn pieces drawn again on a `ModelBiped` inflated by 1, or 0.5 for the leggings, from `armor/<material>_1|2.png`, in the third-person view and in the inventory preview) and the 26 skins (player, 10 armor, 15 mob textures) packed four to a row under `CHAR_Y` in the atlas and the HUD sheet (`atlas::skin_px`, `tools/gen_terrain.py` `SKINS`); Mobs from the real `mob/*.png` skins (`render/items.rs`: `ModelQuadruped`, `ModelCow` horns + udder, `ModelSheep2` + the `ModelSheep1` fleece pass tinted by `fleeceColorTable`, `ModelChicken` with chin, `ModelWolf` with ears, snout, mane, tail and the sitting pose, `ModelSquid` tentacle angles, `ModelBiped` / skeleton / creeper / spider / slime core and face, wolf skin by tame / angry); compiled and `render::player` + `render::items` tests run in a Linux scratch crate (a stand-in `android-activity`), not run on a device. |
 | Debug screen (Info) | type-checked for aarch64-linux-android (`cargo check --lib --tests`), not run (+2 tests in `render/debug.rs`, 2 extended in `options.rs`) | `render/debug.rs`: two translucent panels in the GUI scale for screenshots (left: position, chunk, facing, biome, light, time, aimed block; right: FPS, frame time, screen and scene size with the scene scale, Dynamic Res, MSAA, Post, renderer, graphics and smooth lighting, Performance, render distance, chunks, LoD). Pause menu button `Info: on/off` (`debugScreen` in `options.txt`); while on it replaces the FPS counter and the LoD debug title. See the rendering changelog. |
 | Visual polish (Look) | type-checked on a Linux host (`cargo check --lib --tests`, a stand-in `android-activity`), tests of the touched modules pass there, the WGSL validates with naga and every assembled GLSL with glslang; not run on a device (+8 tests in `render/look.rs`, +1 each in `options.rs` and `atmos.rs`, the sky fan test extended) | `render/look.rs` + the final pass and chunk shaders of BOTH renderers: one `Vibrance` dial (Video Settings, default 30%, 0 = off) scales a grade in the final pass (vibrance, not saturation; a gentle S-curve; warm highlights / cool shadows). `Effects...` (Video Settings) has five switches: Warm Light (golden low sun, bluer shade, faces sink a little deeper), Water Look (depth gradient + sun glint), Glow (soft additive halos on lava, torches, glowstone and the sun only), Motion (off / low / on: leaf sway, motes near flowers and water, light rays at a low sun) and Haze (aerial perspective). Capped: 16 halos, 6 / 14 motes, 40 sprites a frame. `look_*` in `options.txt`. See the rendering changelog. |
 | Audio (M9)           | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+3 tests in `audio/`) | `audio/`: `SoundManager` / `SoundPool`. All 194 effects (80 `SoundPool` keys: `step.*`, `mob.*`, `random.*`, `note.*`, `ambient.*`, `liquid.*`, `fire.*`, `portal.*`, `tile.piston.*`, `damage.*`), 12 music tracks and records 13 / cat are embedded from the b1.7.3 asset index (`tools/gen_sounds.py` -> `assets/sound/`, `audio/table.rs`). Software mixer (pitch by resampling, linear distance gain, pan), lewton decoder, AAudio output via `ndk`; music on a stream thread, one random track 10-20 min apart. Wired: Music / Sound options, footsteps, block break sound (`Block.stepSound`, table read from `Block.java`), note blocks, jukebox records. Not wired yet: every other `playSoundEffect` call of the Java (mobs, hurt, doors, buttons, fire, water, explosions, rain, thunder, cave ambience, pistons, portal). The 12 `streaming/*.mus` files are not b1.7.3 and are left out. |
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ original. Anything that cannot be derived from the b1.7.3 sources is marked
 | Grazing + idle behaviours (2026-10-25) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run; **NOT b1.7.3** (+4 tests in `world/mobs.rs`, +1 in `render/items.rs`; run `cargo test --lib mobs items` first) | Part of the smart animals switch (`animalAi`, on by default; `animalAi:false` gives the b1.7.3 AI back byte for byte). `Mob::idle`: a calm pig, cow, sheep or hen pauses to do something instead of only standing: a cow or sheep on grass **grazes** (3 to 8 s), a pig **roots** on grass or dirt (2 to 5 s), a hen **pecks** (1 to 2 s), and a cow, sheep or pig now and then **rests** (8 to 20 s). Eating and resting stay put, do not turn, and end when a person comes within 4 blocks or the animal is hit. Each wander walk has its own gait (a stroll at 0.6 to 1.0 x the walk, a hen sometimes dashes at 1.5 x). The head is drawn dipped to the ground (`Mob::head`, `Mob::munch`, `render/items.rs::head_dip`) with a chew or a quick peck. The grass is not eaten and nothing lies down. See the gameplay changelog. |
 | Immersive pack (The Forest style, 2026-10-25) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+5 tests in `world/pack.rs`, `menu.rs` flow test extended, carry check in `render/player.rs`); **NOT b1.7.3** | `world/pack.rs` + `lib.rs` + `render/items.rs` + `menu.rs`: with the world's **Immersive Pack** switch on (Create World screen, saved as the 4th line of `<world>/info`; worlds made before it keep the panel), the inventory button no longer opens the inventory: the player takes the pack in both hands (it rises from below, the held item is hidden) and the cloth shows on the flat ground under the crosshair, lime where it fits and red where it does not (needs a full block under 9 samples of a 2.0 x 1.6 footprint, nothing but air or plants on it); a tap, like placing a block, spreads it there (on a red one only a message shows), the button again puts the pack away. The cloth unrolls in the world (0.9 s, a roll that shrinks as it travels), then the screen opens as the cloth: items lie in zones by category (tools & gear, food, materials, other), each at its own size, shrunk together when a zone is crowded; the crafting mat (2 x 2), worn armor and the quick-select row (hotbar) have fixed places. Same `SlotId`s and `Screen::click` as the panel, so crafting, armor, spread-drag, place-one and shift-click work unchanged. Closing, walking 6.5 blocks off or losing the ground rolls it up. A workbench, furnace and chest keep their own panels. Switch off = the old panel. See the gameplay changelog. |
 | Organic mob movement (2026-10-25) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run; closer to b1.7.3 (+3 tests in `world/mobs.rs`; run `cargo test --lib mobs items` first) | Taken from `EntityLiving` of the decompiled b1.7.3 and applied to **every** mob, whatever `animalAi` says. **Momentum** (`Mob::step`): the horizontal speed no longer jumps to the walk speed, it builds up and dies away like `moveEntityWithHeading` (0.546 a tick on the ground, 0.91 in the air, so a hop keeps its run); same top speed; water and lava as before. **Body trails head** (`body_yaw` = `renderYawOffset`): the body follows the way the mob moves (0.3 of the gap a tick, not while knocked back) and stays within 75 degrees of the head, which now turns on its own pivot (`render/items.rs`). **Head tip** (`head_pitch`): a mob that looks at the player or hunts them tips its head up or down to their eye (40 degrees at most, `faceEntity`). Timing is per frame, not per tick. |
-| M14                  | pending | Menus (part 1: title, world list, create world; see above), options, chat, real mob models, player armor: see [`roadmap/gameplay.md`](roadmap/gameplay.md). M10 multiplayer and M13 optimization are out of scope on purpose. |
+| M14                  | pending | Menus (part 1: title, world list, create world; see above), options, player armor and real mob models (both done, see the player model row above and `roadmap/gameplay.md`); only the chat (overlay + bed messages, later) is left: see [`roadmap/gameplay.md`](roadmap/gameplay.md). M10 multiplayer and M13 optimization are out of scope on purpose. |
 
